{"id": "EUVD-2026-103292", "enisaUuid": "6772e8bf-66da-37bd-9186-a8f6e3f21034", "description": "Fleet before 4.83.0 contains a denial of service vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to exhaust server memory by sending gzip-compressed request bodies. Attackers can send small, highly compressed requests with Content-Encoding: gzip to unauthenticated endpoints that expand during decoding, crashing the entire Fleet instance.", "datePublished": "2026-10-17T18:46:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T21:35:14", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/fleetdm/fleet/security/advisories/GHSA-3982-g48v-9rwh", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/fleet-before-4.83.0-denial-of-service-via-unbounded-gzip-decompression"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7fp2-q7fp-2qwf", "CVE-2026-111924"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.36, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ed31c4a4-17cf-31b6-abd1-c2cb26773fd2", "product": {"name": "Fleet", "vendor": {"name": "fleetdm"}}, "product_version": "0 <4.83.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "452565bc-6532-379a-92c5-a9c307e5af4b", "vendor": {"name": "fleetdm"}}], "isExploited": false}